2026-11-06T03:01:35.2628057Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2638730Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2639680Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2640135Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2640477Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2641135Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2641423Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2641652Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2642115Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2642349Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2642483Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2642870Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2643089Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2643286Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2643706Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:01:35.2643884Z 
